            <ArticleTitle>Early Dislodgment and Migration of a Left Atrial Appendage Closure Device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1905-1907</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0002-9149(17)31283-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.amjcard.2017.07.077</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 68-year-old man underwent pulmonary vein isolation with cryoballoon combined with left atrial appendage closure using a LAmbre device. The device was dislodged and embolized early after implantation with no symptoms, and it was retrieved percutaneously. An early in-hospital check of the device position after implantation is important for early recognition of any possible device-related complication.</AbstractText>
